  "id": "COMPOUND:43347 - PROTEIN:78",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Wikstromol may interact with Coagulation factor VII through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Wikstromol to Interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha, which is then targeted by 1-(4-hydroxy-3,5-dimethoxy-phenyl)-2-[4-[3-(4-hydroxy-3,5-dimethoxy-phenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan-6-yl]-2,6-dimethoxy-phenoxy]propane-1,3-diol, a compound that ultimately targets Coagulation factor VII. The second pathway connects Wikstromol to o-Orsellinaldehyde, which directly targets Coagulation factor VII. The third pathway involves Wikstromol targeting Phosphatidylinositol transfer protein alpha isoform, which is then targeted by a compound that also targets Coagulation factor VII. These findings collectively indicate that Wikstromol may exert its effects on Coagulation factor VII through different molecular mechanisms, possibly by modulating signaling pathways or enzyme activities involved in coagulation. The evidence supports a potential role for Wikstromol in influencing coagulation processes, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
